description:
## Goal

Make RuntimeDemand an ordinary change-driven fact calculation and delete the whole-cone pass. A callable edge discovered during demand must become a new dependency, not a reason to discard and replay standing values.

## Fresh signal (release compiler, 2026-08-24)

enum_take_drop_split:

- 660 ms compile session;
- six large demand settlements: 197 members x4, then 237 members x2;
- 6,540 member derivations; the final 237-member ascent contains 1,246;
- external_members=0 throughout.

fz_f98_range_map_converges:

- 103 ms for four executable source lines;
- six large settlements: 55 members x4, then 59 members x2;
- 1,566 derivations; the final 59-member ascent contains 277;
- external_members=0 throughout.

produce_runtime_demand_product settles from bottom, discovers callable-flow resolutions from the result, grows actual_flow_edges, and starts again. Equal-size cones replay when only edge count grows.

## Correct model

Runtime demand is a monotone calculation over executable demand values and source-to-target contributions. Cycles are real and may span the reachable call relation; eliminating replay does not require pretending the dependency component is small.

After prerequisites:

- fz-kdt.44 makes settled reads transitively sound without recalculating unchanged Current readers;
- fz-kdt.45 gives the calculation authoritative ExecutableFacts in the fact graph;
- fz-kdt.47 removes the current dependence on global member evaluation order.

Then:

1. Add RuntimeDemand(ExecutableKey) and exact contribution identities to the fact model, with one authoritative World store and monotone joins.
2. Add one demand formula per executable. It reads Current peer demand/contribution facts, never waits on a cyclic peer, and records every read even when absent.
3. Preserve ExecutableRuntimeDemand as one semantic projection initially unless fz-kdt.34 proves independently moving fields cause false wakes. Do not split cells speculatively.
4. A callable-flow resolution adds an exact Current(RuntimeDemand(target)) dependency and demands its producer. Existing values remain.
5. Artifact/transport consumers wait on transitively settled demand facts.
6. Retraction and ground replacement use the scheduler's rebase path and must be proven explicitly.
7. Delete the cone and PullSession demand authorities.

## Required deletions

- collect_demand_cone and settle_demand_cone;
- DemandConeRetryGuard, DemandGraph, SettledDemandCone, and actual_flow_edges;
- demand-specific dirty/reverse indexes;
- PullSession return/input contribution, contributor, and joined-demand maps;
- replace/recompute demand contribution channels;
- settled-demand callee inventories and bespoke demand invalidation paths;
- whole-cone publication;
- cone telemetry after causal cell telemetry proves the replacement.

Before deletion, census external_members across the full matrix. If the cross-cone external/displacement path remains unobserved, delete it with the cone; if it is observed, its fixture becomes a required retraction/finality test.

## TDD strategy

1. Two-executable acyclic demand chain with exact evaluation counts.
2. Self recursion and two-member mutual recursion: monotone convergence, no waits on peers.
3. Dynamic callable edge discovered after initial values: no bottom reset; only newly affected readers evaluate.
4. Retraction/rebase removes stale contributions and reaches the new fixed point.
5. Demand lattice reaches the same semantic result under several scheduler orders.
6. Existing Range/Map and take/drop/split fixtures prove full behavior.

## Telemetry acceptance

Consumes fz-kdt.34.

- every non-initial demand evaluation names moved input content since its own prior conclusion;
- readiness-only movement causes zero demand recalculation;
- callable-edge growth causes zero value resets;
- changed facts whose stored value is equal remain zero;
- no cone, round, SCC, root, or executable-inventory scan occurs;
- an incremental edit evaluates only formulas in the exact transitive reader closure, even if that closure is legitimately large;
- repeated runs produce identical causal work multisets and byte-identical backend programs.

Use work counts, not time thresholds or a requirement that a cyclic cell evaluate only once.

## Documentation

Replace whole-cone Kleene-settlement documentation with the ordinary fact calculation, contribution ownership, transitive finality, retraction, and dynamic-read invariants. Document everything removed.
